 format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUHARA MANABU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAHI GLASS COMPANY LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRATSUKA, KAZUYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUHARA, MANABU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRATSUKA KAZUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUHARA MANABU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRATSUKA, KAZUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUHARA, MANABU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for manufacturing an electric double-layer capacitor having a low resistance and a large capacitance of more than 10 F, causing little self-discharging, not degrading in capacitance with time, and hardly undergoing deformation of its cell. The body of the capacitor is so constructed that an anode mainly made of a carbonaceous material having a specific surface of more than 500 m&lt;2&gt;/g and a cathode are opposed with a separator interposed therebetween. The body is impregnated with a nonaqueous electrolyte. A voltage 1 to 1.5 times the rated voltage is applied in an unsealed state. The body is kept under a low pressure and the case containing the body is sealed, solving the problems.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention se rapporte à un procédé servant à fabriquer un condensateur double couche électrique ayant une faible résistance et une grande capacitance de plus de 10 F, qui n'entraîne que peu d'auto-décharge, qui ne subit pas de dégradation de la capacitance avec le temps et qui n'entraîne guère de déformations de sa cellule. Le corps du condensateur est construit pour qu'une anode, essentiellement faite d'un matériau carboné ayant une surface spécifique de plus de 500 m&lt;2&gt;/g et une cathode soient placées en position opposée, avec un séparateur entre elles. Le corps dudit condensateur est imprégné d'un électrolyte non aqueux. Une tension 1 à 1,5 fois la tension nominale est appliquée à l'état non scellé. Le corps du condensateur est maintenu à faible pression et le boîtier contenant ledit corps est scellé, ce qui résout les problèmes.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>